                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]Fruit Attacks VR[/b] is a fun wave shooter set on a colorful tropical island. You have to fight against a ton of fruit aliens (or alien fruits?) that want you dead for some reason. There are 3 characters at your disposal. Each has a different weapon that has a unique feel to it. You will have to adjust your strategy depending on what character/weapon you decide to use (or you can switch between them on the fly during the mission). \n\nThis game is simple but very entertaining with plenty of replay value (and achievements). It is tagged as “casual” but it gets pretty damn hard. I am yet to get past wave 20 but I am going to keep trying.\n\nI've experienced some frame drops when there were a lot of enemies on the screen (and in the main lobby, surprisingly enough) but overall the game runs perfectly fine on my GTX970.\n\nI am a little hesitant recommending Fruit Attacks VR at full price of $15 but if you love wave shooters or whenever this game is on sale, make sure to grab it.\n\n[h1]PC Specs[/h1] \n[table] \n[tr] \n[th][u]Hardware[/u][/th] \n[th][u]Type[/u][/th] \n[/tr] \n[tr] \n[td][b]VR[/b][/td] \n[td]Oculus Rift (CV1)[/td] \n[/tr]\n[tr] \n[td][b]CPU[/b][/td] \n[td]Intel Core i7 5820K 3.30GHz[/td] \n[/tr] \n[tr] \n[td][b]GPU[/b][/td] \n[td]Nvidia GeForce GTX 970[/td] \n[/tr] \n[tr] \n[td][b]RAM[/b][/td] \n[td]16GB DDR4[/td] \n[/tr] \n[tr] \n[td][b]OS[/b][/td] \n[td]Windows 10 PRO[/td] \n[/tr] \n[/table]\n\n\n\n[url=http://store.steampowered.com/curator/32296668/]For more [b]Casual Game Reviews[/b] check our Curator's group.[/url]",
